Andrew D. Hilton <adhilton@red.seas.upenn.edu> wrote:
> I believe that when you know the charges on a wand, it does not
> list its BUC status if uncursed, since you cannot know the charges
> without knowing the BUC status, and therefore not listing it
> unambiguosly means "known to be uncursed" when the charges are shown.

Indeed. And this is also true of weapons whose enchantment is known,
but _not_ of armour whose enchantment is known (since you find out
its effect on your AC the first time you try putting it on).

For those of us who like our .nethackrc to colour our inventory
listing to differentiate known-cursed, known-uncursed, known-blessed
and buc-unknown, this is a complete pain, because the regular
expressions must be able to distinguish weapons from armour in order
to do this correctly.

If you play a Priest, the game _never_ says `uncursed'. I haven't
worked out a way to cope with _that_ yet except having a different
.nethackrc for Priest games...
